    <string name="ion_rate_axis">X: Epoch  |  Y: Ion Delay Rate (m/s)</string>
    <string name="ion_help_title">About Ionospheric Delay Rate</string>
    <string name="ion_help_message">IOD (Ionospheric Delay Rate) is computed from L1/L2 dual-frequency carrier-phase epoch differences, reflecting the rate of change of Total Electron Content (TEC).\n\n• Uses geometry-free (GF) combination epoch-difference to eliminate geometric range and receiver clock bias\n• Unit: m/s — ionospheric delay change per second\n• Cycle slips are detected and excluded; RMS is computed per-system\n\nInterpretation:\n  &lt; 0.03 m/s — Stable ionosphere\n  0.03~0.1 m/s — Moderate ionospheric activity\n  &gt; 0.1 m/s — Active ionosphere (solar activity, geomagnetic storm)\n\nActive ionosphere degrades positioning accuracy, especially for single-frequency users.</string>
    <string name="elev_title">Satellite Elevation (°)</string>
    <string name="slip_stats_title">Cycle Slip Statistics</string>
    <string name="slip_stats_axis">X: Epoch  |  Y: Slips</string>
    <string name="slip_title">Cycle Slip Detection (TD-ADR)</string>
    <string name="slip_ts_subtitle">Cumulative over time</string>
    <string name="chip_all">All</string>
    <string name="slip_explain_gf">■ Epoch-diff — Inter-epoch GF check, fast screening</string>
    <string name="slip_explain_mw">■ Dual-freq MW — Needs L1+L2, most reliable</string>
    <string name="slip_explain_pf">■ Poly-fit — Single-freq arc fit, supplementary</string>
    <string name="slip_csr_hint">CSR = Total obs ÷ total slips, higher is better</string>
    <string name="slip_help_title">About Cycle Slips</string>
    <string name="slip_help_body">A cycle slip is an integer jump in carrier-phase observations, caused by signal blockage, multipath, or receiver loss-of-lock.

Three complementary detection methods:
• Epoch-diff — Compares ionospheric residual change between epochs, single-freq capable
• Dual-freq MW — Melbourne-Wübbena wide-lane combination, highest precision
• Poly-fit — 2nd-order polynomial extrapolation on CMC arcs, sensitive to slow drift</string>
