    <string name="td_pr_title">TD Pseudorange Noise (m)</string>
    <string name="td_pr_axis">X: Epoch  |  Y: PR Noise (m)</string>
    <string name="td_cp_title">TD Carrier Phase Noise (cycle)</string>
    <string name="td_cp_axis">X: Epoch  |  Y: CP Noise (cycle)</string>
    <string name="mp_help_title">About Multipath (MP)</string>
    <string name="mp_help_message">MP (Multipath) measures the ranging error caused by satellite signals reflecting off surfaces before reaching the receiver.\n\n• MP1: Ionosphere-free combination of L1 pseudorange with L1/L2 carrier phase — reflects multipath + pseudorange noise on L1\n• MP5: Same combination using L5 frequency (1176.45MHz) — only valid for satellites transmitting L5\n\nInterpretation:\n  &lt; 0.3m — Good, open-sky environment\n  0.3~0.6m — Fair, mild multipath present\n  &gt; 0.6m — Poor, significant multipath\n\nMultipath is primarily caused by buildings, trees, water surfaces, and other reflective objects — especially severe in urban canyons and tree-lined roads.</string>
    <string name="mp1_title">MP1</string>
    <string name="mp5_title">MP5 (L5)</string>
    <string name="gf_title">GF Epoch-Diff RMS (m)</string>
    <string name="td_noise_title">TD Noise (Triple-Difference)</string>
    <string name="td_pr_label">PR Pseudorange (m)</string>
    <string name="td_cp_label">CP Carrier (cycles)</string>
    <string name="td_help_title">About TD Noise</string>
    <string name="td_help_message">TD (Triple-Difference) noise is computed from triple-differenced pseudorange and carrier-phase measurements, eliminating receiver clock error and geometric range to isolate measurement noise.\n\nPR (Pseudorange):\n• Triple-differenced code noise, unit: meters\n• Reflects raw pseudorange precision per constellation\n\nCP (Carrier Phase):\n• Triple-differenced carrier noise, unit: cycles\n• Requires valid ADR (carrier phase) measurements\n• Dashed lines distinguish CP from PR\n\nLower values indicate cleaner GNSS measurements.</string>
